{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/436478-just-for-fun-can-you-give-me-a-werewolf","id":436478,"title":"[Just For Fun] Can you give me a Werewolf...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-10T18:18:30-07:00","id":436478,"title":"[Just For Fun] Can you give me a Werewolf...","content":"... that can survive a fall from orbit?<br /> <br /> That's 60 miles, or about four and a half minutes of falling.<br /> <br /> To survive this, you'll have to be able to survive the following:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Terminal Velocity says that you'll be taking 120 dice of Bashing damage from hitting the ground. You might not want to hit the ground (or figure out a way to tank that much damage).<br /> \u2022 No, there aren't Loci up there. If there were, you'd probably fall through them too quickly to Reach.<br /> \u2022 You are in some sort of spacesuit Fetish that lets you safely ignore the necessary problems with breathing; you get extra bonus points if you forgo this and find some other way to ignore suffocation.<br /> \u2022 Once you get going (i.e. hit Terminal Velocity), you've got to contend with the equivalent of the Heavy Winds tilt at rating 4.<br /> \u2022 You are at about the bottom of the Thermosphere to start with; this means you have to contend with a rating 3 Extreme Environment (it's either ultra-cold or ultra-hot); this lightens up to a rating 1 Extreme Environment once you've hit Terminal Velocity, and have entered the Mesosphere. If you're going without the Suit, increase these values by 1.<br /> \u2022 It's going to take you about two turns to hit Terminal Velocity. The whole fall constitutes a Scene.<br /> \u2022 Bonus points if you can climb out of the crater you'll leave and flip off the asshole that pushed you. <hr /><br /> For sake of argument, you may assume that the Bashing damage from the fall is average (i.e., you take 40 Bashing damage); if you want to open up a dice-roller and use an actual roll, be my guest.<br /> <br /> Oh, and if the character in question doesn't have 5 dots of Glory, this'll get them a dot. Regardless of what they've done before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 03-10-2015, 09:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T18:25:46-07:00","id":436497,"title":"","content":"I'd think with Breath of Air and Cunning 5 you could probably make some sort of cyclone to catch you and float you to safety. A powerful enough Rahu with Crimson Spasm might be able to manage it just by increasing their Stamina enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-10-2015, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T18:29:07-07:00","id":436503,"title":"","content":"Wisdom 5 and Running Silent and/or Glory 5 and Berserker's Might.<br /> <br /> Termina